course: dictionary
lesson: 13104
title: Technical words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to a particular job, such as plumbing, engineering or building trains. You may not meet them in everyday talk, so context is your best friend. Look at what is happening in the text and what the word is joined to or used for.
explain: «The plumber bolted the two pipes together at their flanges.» You may not know flange, but the clues help: the pipes are bolted together at this part. Ask yourself what would fit in that place, then try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: «The train wheel stayed on the rail because of its flange.» A wheel has a job to do, and the flange helps it do that job. When a word names a thing, look for what the thing does. If you are still unsure, a dictionary will settle it.
fact: A flange is a flat rim or edge that sticks out around a pipe, wheel or metal part.
fact: Flanges make a part stronger, hold it in place, or help join it to something else.
fact: A pipe flange is often joined to another flange with bolts.
fact: On a train wheel, the flange is the raised inside edge that keeps the wheel on the rail.
fact: Technical words are used by engineers, plumbers and designers, so context clues are very useful.
exercise: «The plumber bolted the two pipes together at their flanges.» What is a flange? | A tool for cutting pipes | A kind of paint | A type of fish | *A flat rim that sticks out around a pipe or metal part
exercise: What does the flange on a train wheel do? | It makes the train go faster | It cuts the grass beside the track | It is painted to look nice | *It keeps the wheel on the rail
exercise: «The engineer checked each flange for cracks.» Which word names the part being checked? | engineer | cracks | checked | *flange
test: «Each wheel has a flange that stops it sliding off the rail.» Why does the flange matter? | *It keeps the wheel on the track | It makes the wheel bigger | It makes a loud noise | It is decoration
test: «The flanges were bolted together so the pipe would not leak.» What does bolted together suggest? | Left loose on the ground | Painted in bright colours | Cut into small pieces | *Joined with bolts
exam: What is the main job of a flange on a pipe or metal part? | To make it melt in the sun | *To strengthen it, hold it in place or join it to something else | To make it float on water | To change its colour
